abstract: >-
  Designing and building your own geospatial teaching module as a Carpentries-
  style lesson (Markdown basics, creating a lesson repository from the
  Workbench template, working with GitHub Desktop, and adding episodes), with
  additional readings on data curation, FAIR data, metadata and data sharing.
  This module was taught as part of the Purdue-NSF GIS Cybertraining for the
  Social Sciences Workshop, a two-day workshop held at Purdue University in
  2026, to GIS professionals and instructors (Day 2, Putting it all Together,
  for all participants).
